From 86e1aa430b24fc84cdb071ad144b78c183aeb6de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gilli <272772515+amd-cgilli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:06:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [FlyDSL] Add varlen causal conv1d prefill kernel (causal_conv1d_fn
 contract)

Add causal_conv1d_prefill_flydsl_fn, a FlyDSL depthwise causal conv1d for
packed (varlen) prefill batches with the same contract as the Triton
causal_conv1d_fn: one output tensor, conv_states updated in place,
cache_indices / has_initial_state / pad_slot_id / optional bias and SiLU.
Channels map to lanes (two adjacent bf16/fp16 channels per thread for
channel-last inputs with >= 8192 tokens); only chunk zero touches the cache,
so there are no inter-block state races.

Used by the Qwen3.5/Qwen3.8 GDN linear-attention prefill in SGLang.

op_tests/test_causal_conv1d_prefill.py checks Triton and FlyDSL against an
fp32 torch reference (conv_states bit-exact). gfx950, bf16, dim 10240,
width 4, channel-last (model layout):

  tokens               triton us   flydsl us
  16384 (1 seq)          314.8       183.9    1.71x
  4 x 4096               315.2       183.5    1.72x
  1000,63,1000            34.5        27.2    1.27x

Kernel originally by Nikolai Protasov <nprotaso@amd.com>.
